WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.067
To defend himself,

2
00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.867
this painter had to prove

3
00:00:02.867 --> 00:00:04.667
his masterpiece was a fake.

4
00:00:04.933 --> 00:00:05.967
In 1945,

5
00:00:05.967 --> 00:00:07.500
Han van Meegeren

6
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:09.567
was arrested on suspicion

7
00:00:09.567 --> 00:00:10.600
of collaboration.

8
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:11.833
A supposed Vermeer

9
00:00:11.833 --> 00:00:13.433
had reached Hermann Göring,

10
00:00:13.433 --> 00:00:14.633
a leading Nazi,

11
00:00:14.633 --> 00:00:16.267
through an art dealer.

12
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:18.067
His defense was that

13
00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:20.167
he had painted it himself.

14
00:00:20.167 --> 00:00:21.833
But some experts resisted

15
00:00:21.833 --> 00:00:23.100
believing that their

16
00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:23.933
celebrated Vermeers

17
00:00:23.933 --> 00:00:24.767
were forgeries.

18
00:00:25.033 --> 00:00:26.767
He had exploited a gap

19
00:00:26.767 --> 00:00:27.800
in Vermeer’s known

20
00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:28.467
early work.

21
00:00:28.467 --> 00:00:29.933
Religious paintings filled

22
00:00:29.933 --> 00:00:31.400
what experts expected

23
00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:32.400
to find.

24
00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:33.733
A prominent scholar

25
00:00:33.733 --> 00:00:34.600
endorsed one;

26
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:36.400
a museum bought it.

27
00:00:36.533 --> 00:00:38.433
He used old canvases,

28
00:00:38.433 --> 00:00:39.833
then heated modern

29
00:00:39.833 --> 00:00:40.767
resin-based paint

30
00:00:40.767 --> 00:00:42.200
until it hardened.

31
00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:43.367
Cracking that surface

32
00:00:43.367 --> 00:00:44.533
made new paint

33
00:00:44.533 --> 00:00:45.700
look centuries old.

34
00:00:45.867 --> 00:00:46.967
But court-appointed

35
00:00:46.967 --> 00:00:48.067
examiners tested

36
00:00:48.067 --> 00:00:49.133
the materials.

37
00:00:49.133 --> 00:00:50.533
They found evidence

38
00:00:50.533 --> 00:00:52.367
of modern synthetic resin,

39
00:00:52.367 --> 00:00:53.267
matching materials

40
00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:54.633
from his studio.

41
00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:56.067
X-rays revealed

42
00:00:56.067 --> 00:00:57.333
another problem:

43
00:00:57.333 --> 00:00:58.433
separate crack patterns

44
00:00:58.433 --> 00:01:00.267
in the old layers underneath

45
00:01:00.267 --> 00:01:01.833
and the newer painting

46
00:01:01.833 --> 00:01:02.233
above.

47
00:01:02.367 --> 00:01:03.900
The evidence supported

48
00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:04.900
his confession.

49
00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:05.900
An old canvas

50
00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:07.567
did not make the painting

51
00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:08.567
an old master.

52
00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:10.067
The collaboration case

53
00:01:10.067 --> 00:01:10.933
fell away.

54
00:01:10.933 --> 00:01:12.633
The fraud did not.

55
00:01:12.633 --> 00:01:13.467
In 1947,

56
00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:14.700
he was convicted

57
00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:16.333
of fraud and forgery,

58
00:01:16.333 --> 00:01:17.167
and sentenced

59
00:01:17.167 --> 00:01:18.400
to one year.

60
00:01:18.633 --> 00:01:20.300
He had not sold a Vermeer.

61
00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:21.667
He had sold the belief

62
00:01:21.667 --> 00:01:22.767
that it was one.
